                  %mi …
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{(N)Rep}^{\odot}(\ldots)
            generated by cyclic objects.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p The cyclic subcategories are thin: there is at most one morphism between two objects, every morphism is uniquely determined by where distinguished point is sent.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Just as the full subcategory of cyclic pointed
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
